@packages/compiler/src/adapter.sigil import { SigilAgentAdapter }
@packages/compiler/src/report-protocol.sigil import { SigilCompilationReportProtocol }

expand SigilAgentAdapter {
  logic {
    AgentAdapter {
      Supply each adapter the minimal target request, evaluation skill, output
      schema, workspace root, and capabilities declared for its evaluation run.

      Start the provider agent with enforced direct read-only workspace inspection
      and consume its structured event stream.

      Validate structured adapter output before normalizing any finding.

      Reject an adapter that cannot enforce the effective capability contract.
    }
  }

  constraints {
    CapabilityPolicy {
      Every profile declares readable repository scope, executable tool categories,
      network policy, execution budgets, sensitive exclusions, and applicable
      research requirements.

      Direct workspace inspection requires enforced read-only filesystem access, the
      selected workspace as working root, no approval escalation, and ephemeral agent
      state.

      Network access is disabled for every compiler evaluation. Profiles cannot
      broaden this capability.

      An adapter capability mismatch fails the required evaluation rather than
      broadening access.
    }

    EvidenceThreshold {
      An error identifies a violated rule or contradictory contract and provides
      reproducible deterministic or repository evidence.

      A warning cites concrete evidence and states the remaining ambiguity or
      material risk.

      An optimization explains its expected benefit and accepted trade-off.

      Hidden reasoning is never required or retained as diagnostic evidence.
    }

    CompilationDiagnostic {
      Evaluation skills may propose findings but cannot redefine compiler severities,
      diagnostic identity, lifecycle, or compilation color.

      A finding whose rule code is not declared by its evaluation skill is rejected.

      Required evaluator disagreement produces a warning until the conflict is
      resolved.

      Green permits no warning waiver.
    }
  }

  decisions {
    ProviderNeutralEvaluation {
      Decision: Let the compiler own the evaluation protocol, diagnostic schema, and
      native skill-package contract while adapters map enforced direct workspace
      inspection and structured events to provider capabilities.

      Scope: Governs every agent and evaluation skill integration.

      Trade-offs: Provider-specific sandbox, working-directory, event-stream, and
      usage controls require explicit adapter mapping.

      Consequences: Changing providers does not change compiler semantics.
    }

    EvidenceBackedDiagnostics {
      Decision: Allow only evidence-backed errors and warnings to affect compilation
      color.

      Scope: Governs deterministic, model-assisted, repository, and experimental
      findings.

      Trade-offs: Some plausible concerns remain informational until sufficient
      evidence exists.

      Consequences: Unsupported model claims cannot block progress toward green.
    }

    StableDiagnosticLifecycle {
      Decision: Derive stable diagnostic fingerprints from rule, stage, subject, and
      location facts and compare them across runs.

      Scope: Governs report comparison and editor progress feedback.

      Trade-offs: Rules must define stable semantic subjects independently from
      message wording.

      Consequences: Users can distinguish new, unchanged, resolved, and regressed
      findings.
    }
  }

  cases {
    AgentAdapter {
      A required adapter that cannot enforce the configured network policy fails its
      evaluation and produces red.

      A required adapter that cannot enforce direct read-only workspace access fails
      before invoking its evaluator.

      Invalid or unsupported adapter output cannot introduce an error or warning.

      An undeclared diagnostic code is rejected before it can affect compilation
      color.
    }

    EvaluatorDisagreement {
      Two required evaluators reaching materially incompatible findings produce a
      compiler warning and yellow status.
    }
  }
}
